<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deportation of Armenians to New Julfa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1604">1604</a>–<a href="/years/1605">1605</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-julfa">New Julfa</a> was the forced relocation of Armenians from Julfa and other districts by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> in 1604–1605. Resettled in a new quarter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>, the Armenian merchants of New Julfa became central to Safavid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> and long-distance trade, linking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> to markets from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div>
